# The Frugal Architect Agent

An advisory agent on [Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime](https://aws.amazon.com/bedrock/agentcore/) that evaluates software projects against **The Frugal Architect** — the 7 Laws of Frugal Architecture by Werner Vogels (https://thefrugalarchitect.com/laws/).

> **Attribution**: The 7 Laws of Frugal Architecture are the intellectual property of Werner Vogels / The Frugal Architect. Every scorecard and response produced by this agent attributes the laws accordingly. This agent does not claim authorship of the laws.

> **Advisory only (v1)**: This agent reads and recommends. It does NOT modify code, open PRs, or call AWS account/cost APIs. It produces a roadmap; a human engineer implements it.

---

## Interaction modes

| Mode | How to invoke | Description |
|---|---|---|
| **CODEBASE REVIEW** | Connect a repo, then ask "Review my repo" | Full IaC + app-code analysis → Frugal Architecture Scorecard |
| **DESIGN REVIEW** | Describe your system when no repo is connected | Consultative probing questions against all 7 laws |
| **DECISION CHECK** | "Evaluate this decision: [description]" | Evaluate a specific architecture choice against the most relevant laws |
| **TEACH** | "Explain Law III" or "What is Law V?" | Grounded, attributed explanation of any of the 7 laws |

---

## Setup

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.12+
- Node.js 22+ (for CDK infra)
- AWS CLI configured with appropriate credentials
- An AWS account with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore enabled
- Docker (for container builds)

### 1. Clone and install Python dependencies

```bash
git clone <repo-url>
cd frugal-architect-agent

# Install runtime deps
pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt

# Install dev deps (local development only)
pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-dev.txt
```

> **First-time setup**: The `requirements.txt` and `requirements-dev.txt` files contain
> `PLACEHOLDER` hashes that must be replaced before use. Run:
> ```bash
> pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
> pip-compile --generate-hashes requirements-dev.in -o requirements-dev.txt
> ```

### 2. Deploy infrastructure

```bash
cd infra
npm install
npm run deploy:ecr          # Creates ECR repository
npm run deploy:monitoring   # Creates CloudWatch dashboard + alarms
```

### 3. Pin the Dockerfile base image digest

Before building the production image, pin the base image SHA:

```bash
docker pull python:3.12-slim
DIGEST=$(docker inspect --format='{{index .RepoDigests 0}}' python:3.12-slim | cut -d@ -f2)
# Edit Dockerfile: replace sha256:REPLACE_WITH_PINNED_DIGEST with $DIGEST
```

### 4. Build and push the container image

```bash
ECR_URI=$(aws ecr describe-repositories \
  --repository-names frugal-architect-agent \
  --query 'repositories[0].repositoryUri' --output text)
GIT_SHA=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)

aws ecr get-login-password | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin "$ECR_URI"

docker buildx build \
  --platform linux/amd64,linux/arm64 \
  -t "${ECR_URI}:${GIT_SHA}" \
  -t "${ECR_URI}:latest" \
  --push .
```

### 5. Deploy to AgentCore

```bash
aws bedrock-agentcore create-agent \
  --agent-name frugal-architect-agent-prod \
  --container-image "${ECR_URI}:${GIT_SHA}" \
  --agent-descriptor file://agentcore.json \
  --environment-variables \
    AGENT_MODEL_ID=<bedrock-model-id> \
    MODEL_PRICE_PER_TOKEN=<price> \
    OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=<otlp-endpoint>
```

---

## Configuration reference

All configuration is injected as environment variables at deployment time. No values are hardcoded in source code or the Dockerfile.

| Variable | Required | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `AGENT_MODEL_ID` | **Yes** | — | Bedrock model ID (e.g. `anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0`) |
| `MODEL_PRICE_PER_TOKEN` | **Yes** | — | Cost per token in USD (used for cost-per-run metric) |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | **Yes** | — | OTLP endpoint for traces and metrics |
| `RUBRIC_PATH` | No | `agent/rubric.yaml` | Path to the rubric file inside the container |
| `SCAN_FILE_LIMIT` | No | `500` | Max files scanned per run (bounds token cost, ADR-007) |
| `SCAN_TOKEN_BUDGET` | No | `100000` | Max tokens consumed by scan per run (ADR-007) |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | No | `frugal-architect-agent` | OTEL service name for traces |
| `AGENTCORE_MEMORY_ID` | No | — | AgentCore Memory ID (injected by platform when memory is enabled) |
| `AGENTCORE_MEMORY_REGION` | No | — | AWS region for AgentCore Memory |

The agent **fails at startup with a clear error** if any Required variable is missing — never at first invocation.

---

## OTEL traces and metrics

The agent exports distributed traces and metrics via OTEL to AgentCore Observability / CloudWatch:

| Signal | Metric / span name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Trace | `invocation` | End-to-end per-invocation span |
| Trace | `tool.<name>` | Per-tool-call span |
| Trace | `model.invoke` | Per-model-call span |
| Metric | `invocation.duration_ms` | End-to-end latency |
| Metric | `model.tokens_input` | Input tokens per call |
| Metric | `model.tokens_output` | Output tokens per call |
| Metric | `model.cost_usd` | Estimated cost per run |
| Metric | `tool.<name>.duration_ms` | Per-tool latency |
| Metric | `tool.<name>.calls` | Per-tool call count |

**Viewing traces**: Open CloudWatch → X-Ray traces → search by service name `frugal-architect-agent`.

**Viewing metrics**: Open the `frugal-architect-agent` CloudWatch dashboard deployed by the monitoring stack.

---

## Evaluation harness

The offline evaluation harness (`eval/run_eval.py`) scores the agent on:

| Dimension | What it checks |
|---|---|
| **Groundedness** | Every finding cites a real law + real evidence (no fabrication) |
| **Citation correctness** | The cited law number matches the finding |
| **Tool-selection accuracy** | IaC findings use `scan_iac`; app-code findings use `scan_app_antipatterns` |
| **UNKNOWN discipline** | Missing critical info yields UNKNOWN + probing question, not a fabricated score |

```bash
# Run the evaluation harness against a deployed AgentCore endpoint
AGENTCORE_ENDPOINT=<endpoint> python eval/run_eval.py

# Or run against a local Docker instance
docker run --rm \
  -e AGENT_MODEL_ID=<model-id> \
  -e MODEL_PRICE_PER_TOKEN=0.000003 \
  -e OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:4317 \
  frugal-architect-agent:dev &

python eval/run_eval.py --endpoint http://localhost:8080
```

Evaluation results are emitted as OTEL metrics (namespace `frugal-architect-agent/eval`) and as a Markdown report at `eval/results/latest.md`.

